{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>And we shall bring the offering of HaShem, to atone for our souls.</b> We vowed before the count, when we were counted, lest a plague spread among us — and therefore we brought it to the Tent of Meeting. And so we find: 'And you shall take the silver of the atonements and give it for the service of the Tent of Meeting.'" "<b>And we shall bring the offering of HaShem</b> etc. Rashi explained: if we escaped sin, we did not escape evil thoughts. And if you ask: but we find the beautiful woman (יפת תואר) who is permitted in war — what sin and what evil thought is there in this? But we say in the Jerusalem Talmud: the beautiful woman was not permitted to them except after conquest."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:26.340941702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}